            "compact_facts": "[chunk-1] RWKV is a novel model architecture proposed by Bo Peng et al. in 2023. RWKV combines the efficient parallelizable training of transformers with the efficient inference of RNNs. RWKV uses a linear attention mechanism and can be formulated as either a Transformer or an RNN. RWKV scales up to 14 billion parameters, making it the largest dense RNN ever trained. RWKV performs on par with similarly sized Transformers.\n[chunk-2] RWKV is a recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture that performs on par with similarly sized Transformers. RWKV is described as the largest dense RNN ever trained, with models scaled up to 14 billion parameters. The paper 'RWKV: Reinventing RNNs for the Transformer Era' was published in 2023 at EMNLP. The paper was authored by Bo Peng, Eric Alcaide, Quentin Anthony, Alon Albalak, Samuel Arcadinho, Stella Biderman, Huanqi Cao, Xin Cheng, Michael Chung, Leon Derczynski, Xingjian Du, Matteo Grella, Kranthi Gv, Xuzheng He, Haowen Hou, Przemyslaw Kazienko, Jan Kocon, Jiaming Kong, Bartłomiej Koptyra, Hayden Lau, Jiaju Lin, Krishna Sri Ipsit Mantri, Ferdinand Mom, Atsushi Saito, Guangyu Song, Xiangru Tang, Johan Wind, Stanisław Woźniak, Zhenyuan Zhang, Qinghua Zhou, Jian Zhu, and Rui-Jie Zhu. The paper is available on arXiv with the identifier 2305.14978v1. The paper is available on GitHub at https://github.com/BlinkDL/RWKV-LM."
